# ⚡ Privil "Chronos — Study Planner"

> **Your entire academic life, distilled into one stark, uncluttered black-and-white workspace.**
> No sign-ups. No backend. No bloat. Just open the file and start working.


---

## 🎯 The Idea

Every student's day is scattered across five different apps — a to-do list, a calendar, an exam tracker, a habit app, and a meditation app nobody actually opens. **Chronos** collapses all five into a single page, wrapped in a bold editorial design language that feels more like a design magazine than a SaaS dashboard.

It's not trying to be "smart." It's trying to be **fast, honest, and distraction-free** — a workspace that respects your attention instead of fighting for it.

Built in pure HTML, Tailwind, and vanilla JS. **Clone it, open `index.html`, and it just works.**

🔗 **Live Demo:** [chronos-by-privil.netlify.app](https://chronos-by-privil.netlify.app/)
---


## 🖤 Design Philosophy

Chronos is built around a deliberate **brutalist / architectural aesthetic**:

- **Pure black & white** — no color noise, no gradients, no distractions
- **Bebas Neue** for headers and numbers — big, confident, poster-like typography
- **Inter** for body text — clean and legible
- **Thick 2px borders** everywhere instead of shadows or rounded corners — the UI reads like ruled paper or architectural blueprints
- **Numbered navigation** (01–05) — like chapters in a book, not tabs in an app

The result feels less like a productivity tool and more like a **printed planner brought to life.**

---

## 🧭 Feature Walkthrough

### 01 — WORK
Your command center for the day.

- **Focus of the Day** — a single, oversized input at the top forces you to name *the one thing* that actually matters today (borrowed from the "most important task" productivity principle)
- **Study Performance Dashboard** — live-style stats block showing weekly task completion, focus goal percentage, and an editable "Agent Note" summarizing your progress
- **Agent Plan** — a draft queue of AI-suggested tasks (e.g. *"Split Physics Pset 4 into 2-hour blocks to avoid overload before Wednesday's lab"*) that you can **Accept** or **Reject** with one click — designed to simulate an AI co-planner without needing a live API connection
- **Manual Tasks** — a classic checklist with satisfying strike-through animations when tasks are completed

### 02 — WEEK
A full **7-day agenda board**, Monday through Sunday, laid out side-by-side.

- Add unlimited items to any day with a single keystroke (`Enter` to add)
- Click any scheduled item to instantly remove it
- Weekend columns are subtly dimmed (`opacity-70`) to visually separate study days from rest days

### 03 — EXAMS
Deadline and progress tracking for everything that counts toward your grade.

- Add **Exams**, **Assignments**, or **Projects**, each tagged with a bold type label
- Every entry gets a **clickable progress bar** — click to cycle through 0% → 25% → 50% → 75% → 100% → reset, no sliders or forms needed
- Designed for at-a-glance scanning: title, type, and completion state all visible without opening anything

### 04 — HABITS
Because grades aren't the only thing worth tracking.

- Add custom habits (water intake, reading, workouts, whatever matters to you)
- Each habit tracks a **live streak counter** that increments/decrements as you check it off
- **Scratchpad** — a distraction-free, full-height notes panel for brain-dumping thoughts without leaving the app
- **"Get Daily Inspiration"** button surfaces a full-screen motivational quote overlay — click anywhere to dismiss

### 05 — RELAX
Because burnout isn't a productivity strategy. A dedicated recovery suite:

| Tool | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Pomodoro Timer** | Classic 25-min work / 5-min break cycles with play, pause, and reset |
| **4-7-8 Breathing** | A guided breathing circle that visually expands/contracts on a 4s inhale → 7s hold → 8s exhale cycle, looping automatically |
| **5-4-3-2-1 Grounding** | An interactive sensory-grounding checklist for anxiety/stress reset, rooted in a well-known mindfulness technique |
| **Zen Focus** | A hypnotic, continuously morphing black blob animation (CSS `border-radius` keyframes) for ambient, screen-based meditation |

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Markup | HTML5 | Zero build tooling — works by double-clicking the file |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS (CDN) | Fast utility-first styling, no compiler step |
| Interactivity | Vanilla JavaScript | No framework overhead, no dependencies to break |
| Typography | Google Fonts — Bebas Neue + Inter | Editorial, poster-like visual identity |

**No npm install. No build step. No server. Just open `index.html`.**

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

```bash
git clone https://github.com/minmon6767/Chronos-Workspace-Study-Agent.git
cd Chronos-Workspace-Study-Agent
```

Then either:

- **Double-click `index.html`** to open it straight in your browser, or
- **Serve it locally** for a cleaner dev experience:
  ```bash
  python3 -m http.server 8000
  ```
  Visit `http://localhost:8000`

That's it. No `npm install`, no `.env` file, no config.

---

## 🌐 Deploy It Free

Since Chronos is 100% static, you can ship it live in under 2 minutes

